# Overlay and chip UI

Do not use a full-width inverted header for menus or transients.

**Selection overlay** (MODE, BAND, STEP, VOL, BW, BFO, BRT): one 16 px row.

```
TITLE ............... [VALUE]
```

**Font roles**

- **Icom-inspired 16×24** VFO digits (3 px stroke, open counters): frequency only (hero). Each digit occupies a **16 px slot** (`kFreqColOffKW` is left bearing in that slot); the decimal is 4 px. **4 px gap** between slots (1 px if 8 glyphs would overflow). Redraw only slots whose character changed — do not slide the whole row when `1` vs `8`. Packed proportional blit is off. Geometry lives in `fonts/vfo_icom_geom.py`.
- **8×16** Pixel Operator: overlay TITLE / focus / filled chips only.
- **9×16 GOST Type A** (`fonts/GOST Type A/GOST_A.TTF` → `fonts/smeter_gost7x14.py`; `4`/`5`/`S`/`+` hand-tuned): S-meter label + SNR. Full row height. Lab width 30 (`pad2+9+gap1+9+9`). Plain, no chip fill. Wall may shift right — OK to rebalance later.
- **Karat 5×7**: MHz, idle top MODE / BW / TUNED / MUTE (plain, no chip), small secondary.

- Title: normal 8×16, left.
- Leader dots between title and chip.
- Value: rounded inverted chip (`oledPrintModeBadge`, `paintTransient`).
- Chip fill is **+2 px** after the last glyph and **+2 px** before the first (`BADGE_PAD`). **1 px** inset top and bottom of the 16 px row. Same for idle chips.
- Encoder changes **only the chip**, not the title/dots/VFO digits. After **2 s** idle: two fill flashes of **250 ms** with **125 ms** between them, then apply and hide the row. Click confirms immediately.

**Idle chips** (black on filled rounded rect):

- Mode AM/LSB/USB/CW/WFM: top-left. Idle = **plain Karat 5×7** (no chip fill, no outline), centered in the 16 px row. `WFM` is three letters. AM/FM mute replaces mode with **MUTE** (same). Overlay TITLE…[chip] stays **8×16 filled**. VFO and S-meter stay.
- Filter width: top-center on SW **and** WFM (`AUTO`, `110K`, `3.0K`, CW `0.5K`). Idle = plain Karat. With TUNED: shift BW **8 px** left. TUNED idle = plain Karat, right-aligned.
- RADIO overlay (**MODE long** = one-line cave): `TITLE …… [chip]` full settings ring (ex RADIO/DISP/AUDIO/SYS), mode-skip. **MODE short** in this layer = next TITLE only. Encoder turn = VALUE; encoder click / 6 s idle flash = hide. BandDn не вход.
- WFM stereo: hidden until a stereo pilot. Then a **white pictogram** **above `MHz`** (same X as Karat MHz, pages 2–3): `((·))` with inner parens shorter. **No chip fill.** Stays on while the pilot is present — no blink. Not on the S-meter, not to the right of the scale. `MHz` is 5×7 on the bottom pages of the frequency. Idle mode chip on FM is `WFM`.
- S-meter: **fleeing-wall rectangles** (accepted), **7 cells** (8th reclaimed). Optical perspective; trapezoid concept only in `fonts/smeter_wall_concept.png`. Widths `3 3 4 5 6 8 10`, heights `4 5 6 8 10 12 14`, even gaps `2`. Mock: `fonts/smeter_wall_S5.png` / aux `fonts/auxwin1_*.png`. Backup wide-gap: `SMETER_WALL_WIDE_GAP 1` in `defs.h`. Needle `liveX` = right edge of filled steps; analog attack `(d+2)/3` / release `(d+6)/7`. Label (`font7x14smeter.h`, GOST): **plain text, no chip fill**. No second peak. Do not restore 1A/1B. Do not draw trapezoid slants on OLED — they alias on 16 px.
- **Universal indicator** after the wall: fixed slot, **no bracket chrome**. Mux via `g_auxInd` / `g_auxIndSnr`. `AUX_IND_AUTO`: SW (AM **and** SSB) → SNR **same GOST digits** as S-lab; WFM/AM (not SW) FREQOFF ◀/STOP/▶ centered; else empty. Not a MODE chip. RDS not in this pass.
- BAND overlay FM tag is `WFM`, CB is `CB`. No band tag on idle.

Do not add idle VOL, BRT, kHz on SW, or idle BFO `+    0`. VOL/BFO/BRT only in overlay when adjusting.

New settings and transients must use this pattern, not a new menu chrome.
